---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sterile Processing Competency Tracking Software | Certivue"
  description="Track SPD competencies, assess technicians at the point of care with QR mobile forms, and stay survey-ready. Competency tracking built for sterile processing."
  canonical="https://certivue.com/competency-tracking"
>
  <section style="padding-top:140px; padding-bottom:64px; padding-left:20px; padding-right:20px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;">
      <h1 style="color:#fff; font-size:clamp(32px, 6vw, 48px); font-weight:500; letter-spacing:-1px; line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 20px;">
        Sterile Processing Competency Tracking Software
      </h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:17px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
        Replace paper checklists and scattered spreadsheets with a single system that tracks every technician's competencies, documents assessments at the point of care, and keeps your department survey-ready.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:0 20px 80px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:48px;">

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          The competency binder problem
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Sterile processing departments live and die by competency documentation — but most still track it on paper checklists, shared spreadsheets, and binders scattered across the department. When a surveyor asks for proof that a technician was assessed on a specific tray or process, the scramble begins. Missing signatures, expired competencies, and undocumented reassessments become findings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Assess at the point of care, document automatically
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Certivue moves competency assessment onto the floor where the work happens. Educators generate a QR code for any competency; the technician scans it on their phone and completes the assessment on a mobile form — no login required. Every result is timestamped, attributed to the assessor, and saved to the employee's record instantly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Grading that reflects real proficiency
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Certivue uses a four-level scale — A+, A, B, and C — built around how SPD competency actually works. Checklist items and individually scored line items roll up into a single competency grade, and only a passing grade closes an assignment. Anything lower stays in the queue for retraining, so nothing slips through.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          See every gap before a surveyor does
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Dashboards surface exactly which technicians have unstarted, in-progress, or failing competencies, which competencies are coming up for renewal, and which staff need attention. Instead of discovering gaps during a survey, you close them ahead of time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="text-align:center; background:#161820; border:0.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius:12px; padding:48px;">
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 10px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          See competency tracking in action
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:15px; margin-bottom:28px;">
          Give your SPD team one place to document, grade, and prove competency.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#demo"
          style="display:inline-block; background:#22d3c8; color:#0f1117; font-weight:500; border-radius:8px; padding:10px 22px; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px;"
        >
          Request a demo
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
